          <h1>Premature ejaculation: what it means and when to seek advice</h1>
          <p class="in037-b03__lead">Premature ejaculation is common. An occasional episode may not need care, but persistent or distressing concerns deserve a confidential conversation with a doctor.</p>

          <h2>What the term means</h2>
          <p>Premature ejaculation means ejaculating sooner than you or your partner would like. Both physical and psychological factors can contribute.</p>

          <h2>When to speak with a doctor</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>The concern keeps happening rather than being occasional.</li>
            <li>It causes distress or affects your wellbeing.</li>
            <li>It affects your relationship.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>A qualified clinician can discuss possible contributing factors and appropriate next steps. A medical consultation is confidential.</p>

          <p class="in037-b03__actions"><a href="/pages/online-consultation">Online consultation information</a><a href="/pages/contact-us">Contact Kairali India</a></p>
          <p class="in037-b03__source">Source: <a href="https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/ejaculation-problems/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">NHS, Ejaculation problems</a>. General information only; use local Indian healthcare services.</p>
        </article>

      {%- when 'rheumatoid-arthritis' -%}
        <article class="in037-b03 in037-b03--guide">
          <h1>Rheumatoid arthritis: symptoms and why early assessment matters</h1>
          <p class="in037-b03__lead">Rheumatoid arthritis is a long-term autoimmune condition that can cause joint pain, swelling and stiffness.</p>

          <h2>Common symptoms</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Joint pain.</li>
            <li>Swelling in and around the joints.</li>
            <li>Stiffness, often more noticeable after rest.</li>
            <li>Symptoms that can vary over time.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>These symptoms can overlap with other joint conditions. Arrange a medical assessment for persistent joint pain, swelling or stiffness rather than trying to diagnose the cause yourself.</p>

          <h2>Why early assessment matters</h2>
          <p>Early diagnosis helps a clinician plan appropriate care. Before an appointment, note which joints are affected, when symptoms are worst and how they affect daily tasks.</p>

          <h2 class="in037-b03__urgent-title">Get prompt medical care</h2>
          <div class="in037-b03__urgent">
            <p>Contact a doctor promptly if a joint becomes suddenly severe, hot or swollen, or if you feel generally unwell with the joint symptoms.</p>
          </div>

          <p class="in037-b03__actions"><a href="/pages/online-consultation">Online consultation information</a><a href="/pages/contact-us">Contact Kairali India</a></p>
          <p class="in037-b03__source">Sources: <a href="https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/rheumatoid-arthritis/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">NHS, Rheumatoid arthritis</a>; <a href="https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/arthritis/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">NHS, Arthritis</a>. General information only; use local Indian healthcare services.</p>
        </article>

      {%- when 'sinusitis' -%}
        <article class="in037-b03 in037-b03--guide">
          <h1>Sinusitis: symptoms, self-care limits and when to get help</h1>
          <p class="in037-b03__lead">Sinusitis is swelling of the sinuses. It commonly follows a cold or flu and often improves without antibiotics.</p>

          <h2>Common symptoms</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Pain, pressure or tenderness around the cheeks, eyes or forehead.</li>
            <li>A blocked or runny nose.</li>
            <li>A reduced sense of smell.</li>
            <li>Headache, a high temperature or a cough.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>While symptoms are improving</h2>
          <p>Rest, drink enough fluids and avoid smoke. A pharmacist or doctor can advise whether a medicine is suitable for you.</p>

          <h2>Arrange a medical assessment</h2>
          <p>Speak with a doctor if symptoms are severe, persist without improving, keep returning or occur on one side only. Seek prompt care rather than waiting for a routine appointment if you are very unwell.</p>

          <p class="in037-b03__actions"><a href="/pages/online-consultation">Online consultation information</a><a href="/pages/contact-us">Contact Kairali India</a></p>
          <p class="in037-b03__source">Source: <a href="https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/sinusitis-sinus-infection/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">NHS, Sinusitis</a>. General information only; use local Indian healthcare services.</p>
        </article>

      {%- when 'ayurvedic-medicine-for-diabetes' -%}
        <article class="in037-b03 in037-b03--guide">
          <h1>Diabetes: symptoms, testing and ongoing care</h1>
          <p class="in037-b03__lead">Diabetes is a chronic disease that needs proper diagnosis, regular testing and ongoing care from a qualified clinician.</p>

          <h2>What happens in diabetes</h2>
          <p>The body does not produce enough insulin or cannot use insulin effectively, so blood glucose stays higher than it should.</p>

          <h2>Symptoms may be mild</h2>
          <p>Common symptoms include increased thirst, passing urine more often, tiredness, unexplained weight loss and blurred vision. Type 2 diabetes symptoms can be mild, and some people have no clear symptoms when diagnosed.</p>

          <h2>Testing and regular care matter</h2>
          <p>Diabetes is diagnosed by measuring blood glucose, not by an online checklist. Clinician-led treatment and regular checks help reduce the risk of complications affecting the heart, blood vessels, eyes, kidneys, nerves and feet.</p>

          <h2 class="in037-b03__urgent-title">Keep prescribed care in place</h2>
          <div class="in037-b03__urgent">
            <p>Do not stop, reduce or replace insulin or any prescribed diabetes medicine without speaking with the clinician who prescribed it. If you become acutely unwell, use local emergency services or go to the nearest hospital.</p>
          </div>

          <p class="in037-b03__actions"><a href="/pages/online-consultation">Online consultation information</a><a href="/pages/contact-us">Contact Kairali India</a></p>
          <p class="in037-b03__source">Source: <a href="https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/diabetes" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">World Health Organization, Diabetes</a>. General information only; use local Indian healthcare and emergency services.</p>
        </article>
